data.content:
## What Breaks in .NET 11

In EF Core 11 (Cosmos DB provider), the **sync-over-async opt-in is removed entirely**. The provider no longer supports synchronous query/save operations — even with configuration. Calling sync methods like `ToList()`, `First()`, `Count()`, or `SaveChanges()` will throw an `InvalidOperationException` at runtime.

## How to Fix

Convert all repository methods to async:

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

## Key points

- **No workaround** — you can't re-enable sync behavior via `CosmosOptionsExtension` or warning suppression anymore.
- `Add()` remains synchronous (it's an in-memory tracker operation), but `SaveChanges()` → `SaveChangesAsync()`.
- You'll also need to propagate `async/await` up through your controllers/services (all callers in the chain).
- Remove any `.ConfigureWarnings(w => w.Ignore(...))` or sync-over-async opt-in code from your `DbContext` configuration — it will no longer compile or will be a no-op.
